{
"from": 100,
"to": 112,
"text": "The take changes the layout every boot runs, so the windowed stand's boot smoke is listed (`role = 'smoke'`, `env = ['WAYLAND_DISPLAY']`, its binary built by the fast leg's workspace tests) beside the agent-run contract. - `bash scripts/agent-run.sh run all` runs every blitz-tests reader in the per-package build (writing-mode off), and   `fast` runs them in the workspace build (writing-mode on). So both bodies of the bounds reader are read under the   take's `writing_mode.rs` resolution (test-plan · decision/bounds-reader-bodies-each-checked,   decision/per-package-green-not-workspace-green). - No live leg runs in this chunk. - The audit leg runs locally before the push (security-plan · decision/local-audit-before-push). - Every `git diff` reads against the commit this chunk starts from, `930ac5d6fc9e39677f1bcc6199e92259161fe93b`. - `coverage` and the WPT suites are not run locally. CI's `coverage` job reads the per-crate floors on the pushed   HEAD, inside the `ci.py` entry's green; the trial never ran it. WPT is report-only on the fork (test-plan ·   decision/fork-wpt-reading-report-only). - The step-6 control is a one-shot `gate.py control`, never an entry (it mutates source)."
}
],
